# First run: the computer route is named, Check again sits under it, and when
# no server has arrived the banner that says so carries Check again over the
# address field, instead of leaving the owner to type the address twice.
wait-for Connect Readeck
expect kobo connect readeck
tap Check again
wait-for No server has arrived
clean
shot readeck-check-again
expect https://readeck.example
clean
shot readeck-server
expect Step 1 of 3
expect Server address
tap-id server-address
wait-for Readeck server address
type https://read.example
expect https://read.example
clean
shot readeck-address-typed
tap Next
wait-for Account key
expect Step 2 of 3
clean
shot readeck-token
tap Use phone
wait-for Opens the API token page
clean
shot readeck-phone
tap Back
wait-for Account key
# The token is typed hidden, counted, and Show reads it back once.
tap-id credential.enter
wait-idle
type abc
expect 3 characters entered
expect-missing abc
tap Show
wait-for Hide
expect abc
clean
shot readeck-token-shown
# Saved, the first refresh goes to the server. The sweep has no Readeck at
# that address, so the inbox says it did not answer instead of claiming the
# inbox is empty, and offers Try again.
tap Save
wait 10000
wait-for did not answer
expect Try again
expect-missing inbox is empty
clean
shot readeck-first-refresh-failed
# The server is kept: after a restart the app opens on the inbox, not setup.
restart
wait 10000
wait-for did not answer
expect-missing Connect Readeck
